1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,922
A carrom striker hits a still coin.

2
00:00:02,922 --> 00:00:05,751
The striker slows, the coin shoots away.

3
00:00:05,751 --> 00:00:07,916
A gun kicks back as it fires.

4
00:00:08,316 --> 00:00:10,943
Something passes from
one body to the other.

5
00:00:10,943 --> 00:00:12,522
And none of it is lost.

6
00:00:12,972 --> 00:00:14,896
Aarav coasts home on his bike.

7
00:00:14,896 --> 00:00:17,887
His friend, on a skateboard,
grabs the carrier.

8
00:00:18,237 --> 00:00:19,264
Nobody brakes.

9
00:00:19,264 --> 00:00:21,289
But now they both roll slower.

10
00:00:21,289 --> 00:00:24,542
Can we predict the new
speed, with no speedometer?

11
00:00:25,042 --> 00:00:26,410
One law answers it.

12
00:00:26,410 --> 00:00:27,588
Let us find it.

13
00:00:28,238 --> 00:00:31,309
Start with momentum,
from episode fifty four.

14
00:00:31,309 --> 00:00:32,469
p equals m v.

15
00:00:32,819 --> 00:00:35,245
It is a vector, along the velocity.

16
00:00:35,245 --> 00:00:37,720
Its unit is kilogram metre per second.

17
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:41,063
A system is the group of bodies we watch.

18
00:00:41,063 --> 00:00:42,441
Here, two carts.

19
00:00:42,441 --> 00:00:44,720
Forces between them are internal.

20
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:47,010
A push from outside is external.

21
00:00:47,410 --> 00:00:52,026
The law: if no net external force
acts on a system, its total momentum

22
00:00:52,026 --> 00:00:53,153
stays constant.

23
00:00:53,803 --> 00:00:57,648
Cart A, three kilograms, rolls
at four metres per second.

24
00:00:57,648 --> 00:01:00,132
Cart B, one kilogram, is at rest.

25
00:01:00,482 --> 00:01:02,791
A has twelve units of momentum.

26
00:01:02,791 --> 00:01:03,839
B has zero.

27
00:01:03,839 --> 00:01:05,432
The total is twelve.

28
00:01:05,832 --> 00:01:07,698
They hit, and stick together.

29
00:01:07,698 --> 00:01:10,711
Now they share one speed,
three metres per second.

30
00:01:11,111 --> 00:01:12,536
A drops to nine.

31
00:01:12,536 --> 00:01:14,016
B rises to three.

32
00:01:14,016 --> 00:01:14,977
The total?

33
00:01:14,977 --> 00:01:16,104
Still twelve.

34
00:01:16,504 --> 00:01:21,270
On the graph, A's line falls, B's
line rises, and the total stays flat.

35
00:01:21,670 --> 00:01:22,720
Slow-mo replay.

36
00:01:22,720 --> 00:01:25,047
Freeze in the middle of the crash.

37
00:01:25,397 --> 00:01:26,725
B pushes A back.

38
00:01:26,725 --> 00:01:28,207
A pushes B forward.

39
00:01:28,207 --> 00:01:31,583
Equal forces, opposite
ways, for the same time.

40
00:01:31,983 --> 00:01:34,803
So whatever momentum A loses, B gains.

41
00:01:34,803 --> 00:01:36,208
Nothing leaks out.

42
00:01:36,808 --> 00:01:38,776
Now fit a spring bumper on B.

43
00:01:38,776 --> 00:01:42,091
This time A slows to two,
and B shoots off at six.

44
00:01:42,491 --> 00:01:44,575
A loses six, B gains six.

45
00:01:44,575 --> 00:01:45,659
Twelve again.

46
00:01:46,259 --> 00:01:47,159
Your turn.

47
00:01:47,156 --> 00:01:51,077
Both carts start at rest, a
squeezed spring between them.

48
00:01:51,077 --> 00:01:51,977
Let go.

49
00:01:51,819 --> 00:01:54,048
What is the total momentum now?

50
00:01:54,048 --> 00:01:55,368
Pause and decide.

51
00:01:58,368 --> 00:01:59,268
Zero!

52
00:01:58,984 --> 00:02:00,568
It was zero before.

53
00:02:00,568 --> 00:02:03,394
A carries minus three, B plus three.

54
00:02:03,394 --> 00:02:04,461
They cancel.

55
00:02:05,111 --> 00:02:07,468
Now let's prove it, one step at a time.

56
00:02:07,818 --> 00:02:08,718
Step one.

57
00:02:08,688 --> 00:02:12,157
In the crash, B pushes A with a force FAB.

58
00:02:12,157 --> 00:02:14,035
A pushes B with FBA.

59
00:02:14,785 --> 00:02:15,691
Step two.

60
00:02:15,691 --> 00:02:19,247
By the third law, FAB equals minus FBA.

61
00:02:19,997 --> 00:02:21,004
Step three.

62
00:02:21,004 --> 00:02:23,880
Both act for the same time, delta t.

63
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:27,030
Force times time is
the change in momentum.

64
00:02:27,780 --> 00:02:28,755
Step four.

65
00:02:28,755 --> 00:02:30,424
Add the two changes.

66
00:02:30,424 --> 00:02:34,771
The forces cancel, so delta
p A plus delta p B is zero.

67
00:02:35,521 --> 00:02:36,450
Step five.

68
00:02:36,450 --> 00:02:39,526
So the total after
equals the total before.

69
00:02:39,526 --> 00:02:41,736
p A plus p B stays constant.

70
00:02:42,486 --> 00:02:45,321
It works for every
collision, sticky or bouncy.

71
00:02:45,921 --> 00:02:47,100
Remember this.

72
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:50,891
No net external force, no
change in total momentum.

73
00:02:51,591 --> 00:02:53,811
Now, why does a gun kick back?

74
00:02:53,811 --> 00:02:54,868
Link by link.

75
00:02:55,218 --> 00:02:57,623
Before firing, both are at rest.

76
00:02:57,623 --> 00:02:59,268
Total momentum, zero.

77
00:02:59,668 --> 00:03:02,832
Gases push the bullet
forward and the gun back.

78
00:03:02,832 --> 00:03:05,673
Internal forces, so the total stays zero.

79
00:03:06,073 --> 00:03:10,236
The bullet carries momentum forward,
so the gun carries the same amount

80
00:03:10,236 --> 00:03:11,136
back.

81
00:03:11,363 --> 00:03:13,240
Light bullet, huge speed.

82
00:03:13,240 --> 00:03:15,014
Heavy gun, small speed.

83
00:03:15,014 --> 00:03:16,483
That is the recoil.

84
00:03:17,083 --> 00:03:18,194
Side by side.

85
00:03:18,194 --> 00:03:20,572
Left: two carts push each other.

86
00:03:20,572 --> 00:03:24,060
Internal forces only, so
the total stays the same.

87
00:03:24,460 --> 00:03:26,872
Right: your hand pushes both carts.

88
00:03:26,872 --> 00:03:29,491
An external force, so the total grows.

89
00:03:30,091 --> 00:03:31,188
Now you try.

90
00:03:31,188 --> 00:03:33,924
A ball falls freely toward the ground.

91
00:03:33,924 --> 00:03:36,213
Is the ball's momentum conserved?

92
00:03:36,213 --> 00:03:37,576
Pause and decide.

93
00:03:40,776 --> 00:03:41,676
No!

94
00:03:41,246 --> 00:03:44,085
Gravity is an external force on the ball.

95
00:03:44,085 --> 00:03:48,394
Take ball plus Earth as the
system, and the total is conserved.

96
00:03:49,044 --> 00:03:50,779
Now, one worked example.

97
00:03:51,129 --> 00:03:55,619
Aarav and his bike, eighty kilograms,
coast at five metres per second.

98
00:03:55,619 --> 00:03:59,465
His friend on a skateboard,
forty five kilograms, grabs on.

99
00:03:59,465 --> 00:04:01,090
Find their shared speed.

100
00:04:01,590 --> 00:04:04,980
Before: Aarav has eighty
times five, four hundred.

101
00:04:04,980 --> 00:04:06,453
The friend has zero.

102
00:04:06,453 --> 00:04:07,965
Total, four hundred.

103
00:04:08,715 --> 00:04:13,514
After: one body of one hundred and
twenty five kilograms, moving at v.

104
00:04:14,264 --> 00:04:15,903
Momentum is conserved.

105
00:04:15,903 --> 00:04:19,266
So one twenty five times
v equals four hundred.

106
00:04:20,016 --> 00:04:22,572
v is three point two metres per second.

107
00:04:22,572 --> 00:04:25,072
Not lost, just shared with more mass.

108
00:04:25,722 --> 00:04:27,187
Now, the exam trap.

109
00:04:27,537 --> 00:04:30,301
Many students add
momenta as plain numbers.

110
00:04:30,301 --> 00:04:33,477
After the spring push,
three plus three is six.

111
00:04:33,877 --> 00:04:35,761
But momentum is a vector.

112
00:04:35,761 --> 00:04:37,102
Left is negative.

113
00:04:37,102 --> 00:04:40,766
Minus three plus three is
zero, the same as before.

114
00:04:41,416 --> 00:04:42,915
Where is this asked?

115
00:04:42,915 --> 00:04:45,942
In recoil, explosion and
collision numericals.

116
00:04:46,542 --> 00:04:47,751
Exam level now.

117
00:04:47,751 --> 00:04:52,769
A six kilogram shell moves at ten i
metres per second, and bursts in two.

118
00:04:52,769 --> 00:04:55,882
The two kilogram piece
flies off at thirty j.

119
00:04:55,882 --> 00:04:58,310
Find the speed of the other piece.

120
00:04:58,310 --> 00:04:59,569
Pause and solve.

121
00:05:04,969 --> 00:05:06,307
The answer is B.

122
00:05:06,307 --> 00:05:08,753
Fifteen root two metres per second.

123
00:05:09,253 --> 00:05:11,403
The burst forces are internal.

124
00:05:11,403 --> 00:05:13,992
So the total momentum stays sixty i.

125
00:05:14,492 --> 00:05:16,831
The small piece carries sixty j.

126
00:05:16,831 --> 00:05:20,809
So the four kilogram piece
carries sixty i minus sixty j.

127
00:05:21,309 --> 00:05:24,117
So v two is fifteen i minus fifteen j.

128
00:05:24,117 --> 00:05:27,551
Its speed is fifteen root
two, about twenty one.

129
00:05:28,151 --> 00:05:29,612
Here is your recap.

130
00:05:29,612 --> 00:05:31,114
Screenshot this card.

131
00:05:34,314 --> 00:05:36,245
Can you answer these without help?

132
00:05:36,645 --> 00:05:37,545
One.

133
00:05:37,164 --> 00:05:39,198
Aarav's friend grabs his bike.

134
00:05:39,198 --> 00:05:41,192
Why do they both slow down?

135
00:05:42,092 --> 00:05:42,992
Two.

136
00:05:42,668 --> 00:05:47,198
Why can forces inside a crash
never change the total momentum?

137
00:05:48,098 --> 00:05:48,998
Three.

138
00:05:48,689 --> 00:05:51,341
Why does a gun kick back when it fires?

139
00:05:52,241 --> 00:05:56,069
Next time: a block on a rough
floor has four forces on it.

140
00:05:56,069 --> 00:05:57,637
Can you find them all?

141
00:05:57,637 --> 00:05:58,843
Free-body diagrams.
